// AurOS: automatic security updates for everything EXCEPT the kernel,
// grub and shim. Found by review on 2026-09-26, before anything shipped:
//
//  - a kernel update runs zz-update-grub, which regenerates
//    /boot/grub/grub.cfg with grub-mkconfig -- and build/mkimage writes
//    that file by hand. AurOS's start-up menu, its "Put Windows back"
//    entry and its Windows entry would all disappear on the first
//    security update, with nothing on screen to connect the two.
//  - a grub or shim update runs grub-install, which by default adds its
//    own firmware entry at the head of BootOrder. BootOrder is written
//    only by `aurfirst confirm`: on a machine whose person said AurOS
//    does not work, that would make AurOS the default anyway.
//
// These stay out until update-grub regenerates AurOS's own menu and
// grub-install is told to leave NVRAM alone. docs/issues/v3/STATUS.md, 7.4.
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
    "linux-";
    "grub";
    "shim";
};
